---
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '@config/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`The terms governing your use of ${SITE.domain}, including acceptable use, intellectual property, affiliate relationships and limitation of liability.`}
  effectiveDate={LEGAL.effectiveDate}
  lastUpdated={LEGAL.lastUpdated}
>
  <p class="lead">
    These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of{' '}
    <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong> (the "Site"), operated by {SITE.legalEntity} ("
    {SITE.name}", "we", "us" or "our"). By accessing the Site you agree to be bound by these
    Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptance">1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
  <p>
    By accessing or using the Site you confirm that you are at least 16 years old and have
    the legal capacity to enter into these Terms. If you use the Site on behalf of an
    organisation, you represent that you have authority to bind that organisation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="use-of-site">2. Permitted use</h2>
  <p>You may access and use the Site for lawful, personal and internal business purposes. You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Scrape, crawl or harvest content by automated means beyond ordinary search engine indexing</li>
    <li>Republish, redistribute or resell substantial portions of our content without written permission</li>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of the Site or its infrastructure</li>
    <li>Interfere with, disrupt or place undue load on the Site or its network</li>
    <li>Use the Site to transmit malware, spam or other harmful material</li>
    <li>Remove, obscure or alter any copyright, trademark or attribution notice</li>
    <li>Frame or mirror the Site without prior written consent</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="intellectual-property">3. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    All content on the Site — including text, testing methodology, comparison data, graphics,
    layout and source code — is the property of {SITE.legalEntity} or its licensors and is
    protected by copyright and other intellectual property laws.
  </p>
  <p>
    You may quote short excerpts (up to 100 words) for commentary, criticism or news reporting
    provided you include clear attribution and a direct, followable link to the source page on{' '}
    {SITE.domain}. Systematic reproduction of our comparison tables or review scores is not
    permitted without a licence.
  </p>
  <p>
    Third-party trademarks, product names and logos referenced on the Site remain the property
    of their respective owners. Their use is nominative and does not imply endorsement,
    affiliation or sponsorship unless explicitly stated.
  </p>

  <h2 id="affiliate-relationships">4. Affiliate relationships and compensation</h2>
  <p>
    The Site contains affiliate links. When you purchase or sign up through one of these
    links, we may earn a commission at no additional cost to you. These relationships are
    disclosed on every page containing tracked links and in our{' '}
    <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Commission arrangements do not determine review scores, ranking order or editorial
    recommendations. Our{' '}
    <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> describes the separation between
    commercial and editorial decisions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="no-professional-advice">5. No professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    Content on the Site is provided for general informational purposes only. It does not
    constitute legal, financial, tax, security or professional consulting advice. Software
    pricing, features and terms change frequently and may differ from what is described here.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>
      You are solely responsible for evaluating any tool before purchasing or deploying it,
      and for the consequences of any configuration you implement based on our guides.
    </strong>{' '}
    Always test automation workflows in a non-production environment first.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accuracy">6. Accuracy and availability</h2>
  <p>
    We re-verify pricing and product claims on a regular review cycle, but we do not warrant
    that any content is complete, current or error-free. Vendors change pricing and features
    without notice. The Site is provided on an "as available" basis and we do not guarantee
    uninterrupted access.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-party-sites">7. Third-party websites</h2>
  <p>
    The Site links to third-party websites we do not control. We are not responsible for
    their content, products, services, privacy practices or terms. Accessing a third-party
    site is at your own risk and subject to that site's own terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimer">8. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    THE SITE AND ALL CONTENT ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF
    ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF
    MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT
    WARRANT THAT THE SITE WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, SECURE OR ERROR-FREE.
  </p>

  <h2 id="limitation-of-liability">9. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, {SITE.legalEntity.toUpperCase()} AND ITS
    OFFICERS, EMPLOYEES AND CONTRIBUTORS SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL,
    SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, EXEMPLARY OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, INCLUDING LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA,
    BUSINESS OR GOODWILL, ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SITE — EVEN IF
    ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.
  </p>
  <p>
    OUR TOTAL AGGREGATE LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM RELATING TO THE SITE SHALL NOT EXCEED ONE
    HUNDRED US DOLLARS (USD $100). Some jurisdictions do not allow these exclusions, so they
    may not apply to you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="indemnification">10. Indemnification</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {SITE.legalEntity} from any claims, damages,
    losses and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising from your use of the Site,
    your violation of these Terms, or your infringement of any third-party right.
  </p>

  <h2 id="modifications">11. Changes to the Site and Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may modify, suspend or discontinue any part of the Site at any time. We may also
    revise these Terms; material changes will be reflected in the "Last updated" date above.
    Continued use after a revision constitutes acceptance.
  </p>

  <h2 id="termination">12. Termination</h2>
  <p>
    We may restrict or terminate your access to the Site at our discretion, without notice,
    for conduct that violates these Terms or is harmful to other users or to us.
  </p>

  <h2 id="governing-law">13. Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of {LEGAL.governingLaw}, without regard to conflict
    of law principles. Any dispute shall be resolved in the state or federal courts located
    in that jurisdiction, and you consent to their personal jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2 id="severability">14. Severability and entire agreement</h2>
  <p>
    If any provision of these Terms is held unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in
    full force. These Terms, together with our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>{' '}
    and <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>, constitute the entire
    agreement between you and {SITE.legalEntity} regarding the Site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">15. Contact</h2>
  <address class="not-italic">
    <strong>{SITE.legalEntity}</strong><br />
    {SITE.address.streetAddress}<br />
    {SITE.address.addressLocality}, {SITE.address.addressRegion} {SITE.address.postalCode}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.general}`}>{SITE.email.general}</a>
  </address>
</PageLayout>
